        {
          "title": "Exceptions: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Throw Transfers Control",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`throw` jumps up the call stack to the ==nearest matching catch==",
                "The current function **stops immediately**",
                "{red:No normal return} happens"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "throw",
                    "sub": "function stops",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Unwind",
                    "sub": "leave callers",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Match",
                    "sub": "nearest catch",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Handler runs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handler Form",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Handlers tried ==top to bottom==, **first match wins**",
                "List {green:derived} before {red:base}",
                "`catch (...)` takes anything, so put it ==last==",
                "Bare `throw;` rethrows the **original** object"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "try { run(); }",
                "catch (const std::invalid_argument& e) { log(e.what()); }",
                "catch (const std::exception& e) { log(e.what()); }",
                "catch (...) { throw; }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Style and Failure",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Do",
                "Avoid"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Throw",
                  "by value: `throw std::runtime_error(\"x\");`",
                  "extra copies"
                ],
                [
                  "Catch",
                  "`const std::exception&`",
                  "by value: slices"
                ],
                [
                  "Rethrow",
                  "`throw;`",
                  "`throw e;` copies, slices"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Uncaught",
              "text": "Uncaught exception calls ==std::terminate==, which aborts. Even `main()` with no handler terminates, **without guaranteed full unwinding**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Standard Exception Hierarchy and Custom Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Standard Exception Hierarchy and Custom Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Hierarchy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==std::exception== is the root",
                "Virtual `what()` returns `const char*`",
                "Two subclasses: `logic_error`, `runtime_error`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Branch",
                "Members",
                "Flags"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:logic_error}",
                  "`invalid_argument`, `out_of_range`, `length_error`, `domain_error`",
                  "Preventable programmer or contract bugs"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:runtime_error}",
                  "`range_error`, `overflow_error`, `underflow_error`, `system_error`",
                  "Failures found only at runtime"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Other Library Throws",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Exception",
                "Thrown by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`bad_alloc`",
                  "`new`"
                ],
                [
                  "`bad_cast`",
                  "`dynamic_cast` on references"
                ],
                [
                  "`bad_optional_access`",
                  "`optional` without a value"
                ],
                [
                  "`bad_variant_access`",
                  "`variant` wrong alternative"
                ],
                [
                  "`out_of_range`",
                  "`vector::at()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Custom Types and Catching",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Derive from ==std::exception== so one catch handles it",
                "Inherit the constructors with `using`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct DbError : std::runtime_error {",
                "  using std::runtime_error::runtime_error;",
                "};",
                "try { throw DbError(\"down\"); }",
                "catch (const std::exception& e) { }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Catch by const&",
              "text": "Catch by **value** slices the object: ==type and what() text are lost==. Catching by **pointer** is also wrong."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "noexcept and Exception Safety Guarantees",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "noexcept and Exception Safety Guarantees",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. noexcept",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==noexcept== = no exception escapes; if one does, `std::terminate` runs, unwinding not guaranteed",
                "`noexcept(expr)` is the conditional form; `noexcept(f())` is the query operator",
                "Destructors are ==implicitly noexcept==; a throw during unwinding terminates, so catch inside",
                "Moves must be ==noexcept==: `vector` growth uses `move_if_noexcept`, else slow copying"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "void f() noexcept;",
                "template <class T>",
                "void g(T& t) noexcept(noexcept(t.run()));",
                "static_assert(noexcept(f()));"
              ],
              "note": "conditional noexcept wrapping the query operator"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Four Guarantees",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Guarantee",
                "Promise",
                "Typical"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "None",
                  "leaks or corrupt state",
                  "buggy code"
                ],
                [
                  "Basic",
                  "invariants hold, no leaks, state valid but unspecified",
                  "most code"
                ],
                [
                  "Strong",
                  "commit or rollback, state unchanged",
                  "copy-and-swap"
                ],
                [
                  "Nothrow",
                  "never fails",
                  "swap, destructors"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Copy-and-Swap",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Copy",
                    "sub": "temp",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Change temp",
                    "sub": "may throw",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Swap",
                    "sub": "noexcept commit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "T& operator=(const T& r) {",
                "    T tmp(r);   // throwing work",
                "    swap(tmp);  // noexcept commit",
                "    return *this;",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Mark moves and ==swap== `noexcept`; never let a destructor throw."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "RAII and Stack Unwinding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "RAII and Stack Unwinding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. RAII",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RAII==: acquire in the **constructor**, release in the **destructor**",
                "Resource lifetime ==equals== object lifetime"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Resource",
                "RAII type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Heap",
                  "`unique_ptr`, `make_unique`, `shared_ptr`"
                ],
                [
                  "Mutex",
                  "`lock_guard`, `scoped_lock`"
                ],
                [
                  "File",
                  "`fstream`"
                ],
                [
                  "Memory",
                  "`vector`, `string`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stack Unwinding",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "throw",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Leave scope",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Destroy locals",
                    "note": "reverse order",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reach catch",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fully built locals are destroyed in ==reverse order== of construction",
                "Constructor throws: its destructor ==does not run==; built members and bases are destroyed",
                "Raw `new` then a throw leaks: make members RAII"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`new`, `fopen` or `lock()` plus a later cleanup line: a throw skips it",
                "**Never** throw from a destructor"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::lock_guard<std::mutex> g(m);",
                "auto p = std::make_unique<Conn>();",
                "risky();  // g and p released on throw"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Wrap every resource in an object. Prefer standard RAII types over manual `new`/`delete` or `lock()`/`unlock()`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
