            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. std::expected (C++23)",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::expected<T,E>` holds ==either a value or an error==",
                "Check `if (r)`, then `*r` or `r.value()`; `r.error()` gives the error"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::expected<int, Err> parse(std::string_view s) {",
                "    if (s.empty())",
                "        return std::unexpected(Err::NotFound);",
                "    return std::stoi(std::string(s));",
                "}",
                "auto r = parse(s);",
                "if (r) use(*r); else log(r.error());"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Chain without nested ifs: `.and_then(f)`, `.transform(f)`, `.or_else(f)`",
                "`value()` throws ==bad_expected_access<E>== on error",
                "`value_or(x)` gives a default"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Exceptions for ordinary control flow",
                "Dereferencing an expected without checking it"
